G5023.d:
οὗτος, αὕτη, τοῦτο, genitive, τούτου, ταύτης, τούτου, 
 [in LXX chiefly for זֹאת ,זֶה ;] 
 demonstr. pron. (related to ἐκεῖνος as hic to ille),  
this; 
  1. as subst., this one, he; 
  (a) absol.: Matt.3:17, Mark.9:7, Luke.7:44, 45, John.1:15, Acts.2:15, al.; expressing contempt (cl.), Matt.13:55, 56, Mark.6:2, 3, John.6:42, al.; εἰς τοῦτο, Mark.1:38, Rom.14:9; μετὰ τοῦτο (ταῦτα; V. Westc. on John.5:1), John.2:12 11:7, al.; 
  (b) epanaleptic (referring to what precedes): Matt.5:19, Mark.3:35, Luke.9:48, John.6:46, Rom.7:10, al.; 
  (with) proleptic (referring to what follows): before ἵνα (Bl., §69, 6), Luke.1:43, John.3:19 (and freq.) 15:8, Rom.14:9, al.; before ὅτι, Luke.10:11, John.9:3o, Acts.24:14, Rom.2:3, al.; ὅπως, Rom.9:17; ἐάν, John.13:35; 
  (d) special idioms: τοῦτο μὲν . . . τ. δέ (cl), partly . . . partly. Heb.10:33; καὶ τοῦτο (τοῦτον, ταῦτα), and that (him) too, Rom.13:11, 1 Cor.2:2, Heb.11:12; τοῦτ᾽ ἐστιν, Matt.27:46.
  2. As adj., with subst.; 
  (a) with art. 
  (α) before the art.: Matt.12:32, Mark.9:29, Luke.7:44, John.4:15, Rom.11:24, Rev.19:9, al.; 
  (β) after the noun: Matt.3:9, Mark.12:16, Luke.11:31, John.4:13, Acts.6:13, Rom.15:28, 1 Cor.1:20, Rev.2:24, al.; 
  (b) with subst. anarth. (with predicative force; Bl., §49, 4): Luke.1:36 2:2 24:21, John.2:11 4:54 21:14, 2 Cor.13:1.
 (AS)

G5043.d:
τέκνον, -ου, τό 
 (τίκτω), [in LXX chiefly for בֵּן, also for יֶלֶד, etc. ;] 
that which is begotten, born (cf. Scottish bairn), a child of either sex: Mark.13:12, Luke.1:7, Acts.7:5; pl., Matt.7:11, Mark.7:27, Luke.1:17, Eph.6:1, al.; τέκνα ἐπαγγελίας, Rom.9:8; τ. τῆς σαρκός, ib.; in a wider sense (as Heb. בָּנִים), of posterity, Matt.2:18, Luke.3:8, al.; specif., of a male child, Matt.21:28, Acts.21:21, a,l.; in voc. as a form of kindly address from an elder to a junior or from a teacher to a disciple, Matt.9:2 21:28, Mark.2:5, Luke.2:48; τ. μου (= cl. τ. μοι; see Bl., §37, 5), Gal.4:19 (τεκνία, WH, txt.), 2 Tim.2:1. Metaphorical, 
  (a) of disciples (apart from direct address, see supr.): Phm 10, 1 Tim.1:2, Titus.1:4, 3Jo.4; 
  (b) with reference to the Fatherhood of God (see: πατήρ, γεννάω), τέκνα τ. θεοῦ (cf. Isa.30:1, Wis.16:21): Rom.8:16, Eph.5:1, Phil.2:15; and esp. in Johannine bks. (cf. Westc, Epp. Jo., 94, 120),  John.1:12, 1 John.3:1 al.; 
  (with) of those who imitate others and are therefore regarded as the spiritual offspring of their exemplars: Matt.3:9, Luke.3:8, John.8:39, Rom.9:7, 1 Pet.3:6; τ. διαβόλου, 1 John.3:10; 
  (d) as in Heb. (LXX, Jol.2:23, Ps.149:2, 1Ma.1:38), of the inhabitants of a city: Matt.23:37, Luke.13:34 19:44, Gal.4:25; 
  (e) with an adjectival genitive, frequently rendering a Heb. expression, adopted from LXX or formed on the analogy of its language, but sometimes with parallels in Gk. writers (see Deiss., BS, 161ff.): τέκνα φωτός, Eph.5:8; τ. ὑπακοῆς, 1 Pet.1:14; κατάρας, 2 Pet.2:14; ὀργῆς, Eph.2:3. 
 SYN.: see: παῖς. (AS)

G5119.d:
τότε, demonstr. adv. of time, correlat. of ὅτε, 
 then, at that time; 
  (a) of concurrent events: Matt.2:17 3:5 and freq., Rom.6:21; before ptcp., Matt.2:16, Gal.4:8; opposite to νῦν, Gal.4:29, Heb.12:26; ὁ τ. κόσμος, 2 Pet.3:6; 
  (b) of consequent events, then, thereupon: Matt.2:7 3:5 4:1 and freq., Luke.11:26; τ. οὖν, John.11:14 19:1, 16 20:8; εὐθέως τ., Acts.17:14; ὅτε . . . τ., Matt.13:26 21:1, John.12:16; ἀπὸ τ., Matt.4:17 16:21 26:16, Luke.16:16; 
  (with) of things future: Matt.24:28, 40 25:1, 31ff.; opposite to ἄρτι, 1 Cor.13:12; καὶ τ., Matt.7:23, Mark.13:21, Luke.21:27, 1 Cor.4:5, al.; ὅταν . . . τ., Matt.9:15, Mark.2:20, Luke.5:35, 1 Thess.5:3, al. (more frequently in Mt than in the rest of the NT). 
 (AS)

